# Build-context exclusions for every image (plan 8.4 §2.1). Lives at the
# REPO ROOT because that is the build context of all four Dockerfiles
# (infra/deploy/docker/*) and Docker reads .dockerignore ONLY from the
# context root — the first placement beside the Dockerfiles was never
# consulted, and the images job's sentinel scan caught the planted
# apps/web/.env in a web-image layer (2026-08-15, the gate's first real
# catch). ENFORCED, not aspirational: the images job builds with sentinel
# values planted in .env files and scan-image-secrets.sh fails CI if any
# sentinel reaches a layer — removing an exclusion here turns that gate red.
.git
.github

# Env files never enter a build context; .env.example is the documented
# placeholder set and is allowed.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
# The console's Vite profiles are all client-public by design (VITE_* only)
# and the console image build needs them.
!apps/console/.env.*

# Devnet state (keys, chain data) and local stores.
infra/devnet/state/
.pnpm-store/
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/generated
**/test-results
**/playwright-report

# Contracts: the wasm toolchain never enters app images; the artifact is
# built on demand by the bootstrap, not baked (no binaries in git either).
contracts/
